„­bible_version£KJV¤book8§chapter¨sections˜…¤book8§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙpPaul, a prisoner of Jesus Christ, and Timothy our brother, unto Philemon our dearly beloved, and fellowlabourer,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ[and to our beloved Apphia, and Archippus our fellowsoldier, and to the church in thy house:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙGgrace to you, and peace, from God our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book8§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ<I thank my God, making mention of thee always in my prayers,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ\hearing of thy love and faith, which thou hast toward the Lord Jesus, and toward all saints;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‚that the communication of thy faith may become effectual by the acknowledging of every good thing which is in you in Christ Jesus.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙsFor we have great joy and consolation in thy love, because the bowels of the saints are refreshed by thee, brother.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book8§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙYWherefore, though I might be much bold in Christ to enjoin thee that which is convenient,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse	¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙwyet for love's sake I rather beseech thee, being such an one as Paul the aged, and now also a prisoner of Jesus Christ.¦layout ªlast_verse	„¥verse
