„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙRwhich in time past was to thee unprofitable, but now profitable to thee and to me:¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book8§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙMwhom I have sent again: thou therefore receive him, that is, mine own bowels:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙrwhom I would have retained with me, that in thy stead he might have ministered unto me in the bonds of the gospel:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙobut without thy mind would I do nothing; that thy benefit should not be as it were of necessity, but willingly.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book8§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙYFor perhaps he therefore departed for a season, that thou shouldest receive him for ever;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙnot now as a servant, but above a servant, a brother beloved, specially to me, but how much more unto thee, both in the flesh, and in the Lord?¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book8§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ<If thou count me therefore a partner, receive him as myself.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙGIf he hath wronged thee, or oweth thee ought, put that on mine account;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‹I Paul have written it with mine own hand, I will repay it: albeit I do not say to thee how thou owest unto me even thine own self besides.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙQYea, brother, let me have joy of thee in the Lord: refresh my bowels in the Lord.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book8§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙeHaving confidence in thy obedience I wrote unto thee, knowing that thou wilt also do more than I say.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙfBut withal prepare me also a lodging: for I trust that through your prayers I shall be given unto you.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book8§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ>There salute thee Epaphras, my fellowprisoner in Christ Jesus;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ6Marcus, Aristarchus, Demas, Lucas, my fellowlabourers.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ=The grace of our Lord Jesus Christ be with your spirit. Amen.¦layout ‚¤textÙ5Written from Rome to Philemon, by Onesimus a servant.¦layout¥blankªlast_verse